        "name": null,
        "patch_url": null
      },
      "body": "If a flush fails after `PruneOneBlockFile()` clears `nSize`, retrying `pruneblockchain` won't clean up the files. `FindFilesToPruneManual()` skips files with `nSize == 0`, so `fFlushForPrune` stays false. With `FlushStateMode::NONE`, `should_write` is false and the function returns early without ever unlinking them.\n\nIn `chainstate_write_tests.cpp:211`, the retry passes only because it calls `FORCE_FLUSH` instead of `FlushStateMode::NONE, prune_height`.",
